A larger per-CPU TB jump cache (z6ii): 2^14 entries instead of 2^12.

Every indirect branch (a return, a pop into pc, a table branch) looks the next TB up in the vCPU's jump cache
and, on a miss, in the global hash table, and in live view those lookups take a sizeable share of the host
time. The cache's softmmu hash takes the low six bits of the PC
as they are, and Thumb code never sets bit 0, so of 4096 entries the firmware can use about half. Four times
the entries costs 192 KB more per vCPU. A lookup cache only: what runs, and every --vtime run, is unchanged.

diff -ru a/accel/tcg/tb-jmp-cache.h b/accel/tcg/tb-jmp-cache.h
--- a/accel/tcg/tb-jmp-cache.h
+++ b/accel/tcg/tb-jmp-cache.h
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@
 #include "qemu/rcu.h"
 #include "exec/cpu-common.h"
 
-#define TB_JMP_CACHE_BITS 12
+/* z6ii: 14, not 12 (tb-jmp-cache-bits.patch) */
+#define TB_JMP_CACHE_BITS 14
 #define TB_JMP_CACHE_SIZE (1 << TB_JMP_CACHE_BITS)
 
